  <aside class="practice-note"><h2>Learn by changing the request</h2><p>The <a href="/learn/databases/object-storage/sandbox/">object-storage sandbox</a> lets you upload text objects, step through competing conditional writes, complete multipart uploads, recover versions and inspect application protocols. Each lesson explains its starting state and what its model omits.</p><p>For real service calls, use the <a href="/learn/databases/object-storage/practice/">AWS CLI practice guide</a> with your own disposable bucket. The browser never needs your AWS credentials.</p></aside>
  <h2>Sources and model notes</h2><p>The <a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/Welcome.html">S3 service guide</a> establishes the object and bucket model; focused articles link the specific API contracts they use. Our products, recordings and request schedules are teaching examples. We explain documented service behaviour and executed local models separately. General-purpose bucket assumptions do not automatically apply to directory, table or vector buckets.</p>
 </article>
